Z||000001||ChadMan||12-16-1999||09:11 AM||||Holy s**t.  That's the worst Fiero accident I've ever seen.<P>I wonder if he was fibbing about how fast he was going?  Fiero space frames are pretty strong...think about how much force it would take to rip one in half like that.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||12-16-1999||09:57 AM||||Jeez... <BR>I was talking with a guy from work, about Fiero safety. He said he's only known one other person with a Fiero. Seems this guy was on the interstate, and overcorrected, trying to miss a sheet of plywood that had blown off of a truck. He just "turned left", and hit the center wall. At speed. He was out of work, for a while, but lived to tell about it. Said he thought the guy probably would've been killed if he'd been driving something else.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||12-16-1999||11:29 AM||||Wow.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||12-16-1999||04:48 PM||||Chadman, he never says how fast HE was going... he says the truck was doing 50. Familiar road... driving a Fiero... My guess is he was going much faster. Even at the same speed, 50 + 50 = 100. I think the little car did a good job of keeping him alive!!!<P>Just glad nobody else was in the Fiero... and that the curve wasn't from the opposite direction...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero SE||12-16-1999||05:04 PM||||Man, fiero's break easy. Like most toys! hehe. I'm scared to drive mine now. Guess I need to make sure the bolts are tight so if I get hit by a truck it won't get cut in half. That was scary. But atleast the guy was ok. ||||reg||4
Z||000006||M King||12-16-1999||07:57 PM||||This same type of accident happened to a friend of my uncles in Texas. The car broke completely in half. He was in bad shape for a few weeks but he did live! I wonder if they had a prob. with this type of accident?||||reg||11
Z||000007||fiero56||12-16-1999||08:14 PM||||Do you mean "they" as in Fieros, or cars in general?  <BR>Last year there was a bad accident at 725 and paragon rd. Speed limits are 45(725) and 35(paragon). One of the cars was going so fast he couldn't stop for a red light, and hit cross traffic.  The innocent guy died, his car was cut in haf, and parts of the cars ended up in a nearby Ethan Allen showroom. The speeder lived, I don't what they did about it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Scott2M4||12-17-1999||07:23 AM||||I remember that, fiero56.  If I remember correctly, the guy that died was driving an Acura Integra.  Don't remember exactly what leadfoot was driving ...||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||12-17-1999||08:34 AM||||I had to drive past/around the accident on my way home from school that day. I remember there being the front of one car under the stoplight, and one ball of metal laying in the front yard of Ethan Allen. The front showroom windows were broken from debris, and the cars managed to take out a huge steel power pole. That intersection and surrounding streets were closed all day.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||12-17-1999||02:15 PM||||The important thing to remember is that the passenger compartment was still intact.  Long live the Fiero!  Down with Ralph Nader!||||reg||1
